# environments
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# generated model outputs (reproduce with make run-v3 / run-legacy)
data/outputs/

# MATLAB run outputs (regenerated by run_all_scenarios on a licensed machine)
matlab/outputs/*
!matlab/outputs/.gitkeep
matlab/simulink/
*.slxc
*.asv

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# local release bundles
release/
*.zip

# The 3D explorer's built web payload and GLB models are COMMITTED deliverables, not
# scratch output: the web tier must serve from a clean checkout with no build step, and
# tests/test_explorer_drift.py gates them against a fresh build. The standalone project
# ignored them, which was right for a scratch repo and wrong for a shipped one.
# Nothing under explorer/web/ is ignored -- this note exists so nobody re-adds it.

# Vendored third-party browser assets, fetched by scripts/vendor_cesium.sh.
# Build/Cesium is 20 MB across 375 files. It is pinned to the same release index.html
# loads, reproducible on demand, and bundled at desktop-packaging time, so committing it
# would add 20 MB to every clone of a planning-study repository for no determinism gain.
explorer/web/vendor/
